<title>USA: Atlas Air extends B747F contract with CAL.</title>
<headline>Atlas Air extends B747F contract with CAL.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atlas Air said it has signed two three-year contract extensions with China Airlines (CAL) covering Boeing 747-200 freighters it operates for the Taiwan-based airline.</p>
<p>The contracts, both expiring in 1998 and worth about $150 million, have been extended through to 2001, Atlas said.</p>
<p>CAL was Atlas's first customer back in March 1993 when the U.S. carrier launched an 'ACMI' product, which offers customers freighter aircraft, crew, maintenance and insurance on long-term contract rates.</p>
<p>-Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +44 171 542 7706 Fax +44 171 542 5017</p>
